      "message": "fix(2d): judge a picked Circular against its part; Slot shares authored_law\n\nA Circular whose source is a pick of the finished part took\nDepthLaw::None, so a ring typed below its picked floor read clean on the\noperation; with a rotated stock the program sim refuses to judge and\nuncovered() accepts that empty verdict, so the overcut could post.\nauthored_law now judges picks too (Entity | Selection -> Section, Stock\n-> None), and the Slot arm calls it as well, so the one shared law is\nreal code. The Slot's law is unchanged (Section for every part-solid\nsource since #1504 / #1537; part_solid is never true for Stock).\n\nPins: circular_pick_law (picked ring 3 mm below its floor with a rotated\nstock: op gouges, post refused by name on the op's moves; MCP verify\nnames the op's gouge; at the floor clean; a pick off a from-model stock\nnever judged - the part_solid early return's placement), and\nauthored_law_tests (picks Section, Slot through the same law). Decision\nfile: chord-sag readings corrected (64 chords refused at leave 0), why\nContain is not pinnable by integration for a Circular.\n\nFixes #1550\nRefs #1543\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAgjpiZbXSvmXLvdmL",
